my $CODE = <<'END_CODE';
hello world
END_CODE

{
    desc => ': then Escape returns to normal mode',
    description => <<'END_DESC',
Macro: `xt/visual/macros/command_to_normal`

Tests that pressing `:` then `<Escape>` cancels command mode and returns
to normal mode with no side effects.

**initial.png** — Normal mode, cursor at line 1 col 0.

Keys: `:<Escape>`

**after_escape.png** — Back in normal mode. Buffer content unchanged.
No command was executed.
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys(':\e');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_escape');
    },
}
